1
00:00:00,257 --> 00:00:01,357
(Raj:)No, you didn't.

2
00:00:01,358 --> 00:00:03,928
(Raj:)There are millions
of data points there.

3
00:00:03,927 --> 00:00:06,657
(Sheldon:)But, look, an
optical transient.

4
00:00:06,663 --> 00:00:08,263
(Raj:)Yeah, maybe
that is something.

5
00:00:08,265 --> 00:00:10,565
(Raj:)How did you find that?
It wasn't difficult.

6
00:00:10,567 --> 00:00:13,807
(Sheldon:)You know how when you see
prime numbers, they appear red,

7
00:00:13,804 --> 00:00:15,434
(Sheldon:)but when they're
twin primes,

8
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:17,539
(Sheldon:)they're pink and
smell like gasoline?

9
00:00:19,075 --> 00:00:20,505
(Amy(on Skype):)No.

10
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:23,710
(Sheldon:)Oh. I guess I'm
a special boy.

11
00:00:23,713 --> 00:00:26,413
(Sheldon:)You know, sometimes
when a boy is special,

12
00:00:26,416 --> 00:00:28,346
(Sheldon:)he gets a Fudgsicle.

13
00:00:28,351 --> 00:00:31,521
(Sheldon:)Which, by the way, tastes
like the speed of light.

14
00:00:34,224 --> 00:00:36,624
(Leonard:)Thank you for seeing me
on such short notice.

15
00:00:36,626 --> 00:00:38,026
(Dr Gallo:)Ah, it's my pleasure.

16
00:00:38,028 --> 00:00:39,028
(Dr Gallo:)I'm curious,

17
00:00:39,029 --> 00:00:41,859
(Dr Gallo:)are you related
to Dr. Beverly Hofstadter?

18
00:00:41,865 --> 00:00:44,365
(Leonard:)Uh, she's my mother.
You know her?

19
00:00:44,367 --> 00:00:45,467
(Dr Gallo:)No, not personally,

20
00:00:45,469 --> 00:00:47,469
(Dr Gallo:)but I have read
all of her books.

21
00:00:47,471 --> 00:00:49,601
(Leonard:)Well, then you know her
better than I do.

22
00:00:49,606 --> 00:00:51,506
(Dr Gallo:)Well, I'm not so sure
about that.

23
00:00:51,508 --> 00:00:53,908
(Dr Gallo:)But I can tell you
I do not agree

24
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:56,740
(Dr Gallo:)with her theories
on child rearing at all.

25
00:00:56,746 --> 00:00:58,946
(Leonard:)Really?

26
00:00:58,949 --> 00:01:01,679
(Leonard:)Any chance you find them
cold, cruel and unsuitable

